invariant: INV-17
file: src/sha512_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: round_pair keeps the old c and d, which SHA512H2 reads after the add
  writes over cd, in a local of its own, which the compiler must hold in
  memory, where they belong in the block_state (docs/decisions.md 243).
  compress_blocks wipes the block_state alone, so its dead frame keeps two
  working variables of the last block. Every digest is still right.
  bin/sha2_equiv_test copies the stack below each kind of call and looks
  for two 64-bit words in a row that the call computed from its input, the
  working variables after each round among them. The script runs the arm64
  binary under qemu-aarch64. The lane skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    c->before = *cd;
    *cd = vaddq_u64(*cd, c->half);
    *gh = vsha512h2q_u64(c->half, c->before, *ab);
--- new
    volatile words before = *cd;
    *cd = vaddq_u64(*cd, c->half);
    *gh = vsha512h2q_u64(c->half, before, *ab);
